    "title": "How Does Amazon's Robot Feel What It Grabs? 🤖 #shorts",
    "description": "This robot can feel what it's grabbing. 🤖\n\nAmazon's Vulcan works with the fabric bins in its warehouse pods, which are packed tight. Cameras alone can't tell how hard to push, so Vulcan's gripper has force sensors that work like fingertips: it nudges other items aside and slides the new one in without crushing anything. Amazon says it can pick and stow about 75% of the item types in its fulfillment centers at speeds close to a human worker, and it takes the top and bottom shelves so people don't need ladders.\n\nA coworker with a gentle touch, and zero coffee breaks. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
